;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Plan: tighten the LangSec '26 cbcl-arena evaluation along seven axes
;; flagged in eval-review (2026-05-01).
;;
;; Load-bearing claims (would tighten or close existing CIs):
;;   E1. Live-LLM bindings on Yao / Auction / Dining (only PSI is wired).
;;   E2. Sonnet 4.6 / GPT-4.1 columns of tab:mcp-attacks (currently blank).
;;   E3. Vanilla configuration sweep — regex-breadth distribution.
;;   E4. Bump PSI live-LLM N=20 -> 100+ (CIs currently overlap).
;;
;; Explicit contract gaps (ZC: pending or design-implied):
;;   E5. Ultimatum operator + attackers + agent (dialect already shipped).
;;   E6. Non-stationary attacker library (last-K success bandit).
;;   E7. Coalition attacks for DC (current 0-row is uninformative under
;;       single-attacker threat model).
;;
;; Outside this plan (cited for clarity):
;;   - 01-A/D-protocol + 01-A/D-confusion: cbcl-mcp, not arena.
;;   - Demo 4 corrupt-auctioneer / MPC: standalone piece.
;;   - R5 Lean mechanisation: lean-cbcl.
;;   - arena.nicolaos.org field test: integration work.
;;
;; Architecture spine. The single highest-leverage refactor is to
;; decompose the monolithic GLM seats (`glm/disciplined.rs`,
;; `glm/cbcl_native.rs`) into:
;;
;;   - `LlmBackend` trait: the chat() RPC, swappable across providers
;;     (Z.ai GLM-5.1, Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT-4.1).
;;   - `ProtocolAdapter` trait: per-operator dialect plumbing — system
;;     prompt template, tool-defs, phase machine, message parsing,
;;     canonical-form hashing, caused-by resolution.
;;   - `DisciplinedSeat<P, B>` and `CbclNativeSeat<P, B>`: generic over
;;     both axes. The current GLM-PSI seat becomes
;;     DisciplinedSeat<PsiAdapter, GlmBackend>.
;;
;; This refactor is the prerequisite for E1 (per-operator adapters) and
;; E2 (per-backend impls), and once it lands the matrix is just data.
;;
;; Dependency layering:
;;   W1: foundation refactor (trait-llm-backend, trait-protocol-adapter)
;;   W2: per-operator adapters (psi/yao/auction/dining), parallel after W1
;;   W3: per-backend impls (claude/gpt), parallel after W1
;;   W4: live-LLM cells matrix run + transcript emission (after W2 + W3)
;;   W5: vanilla regex sweep (independent of refactor)
;;   W6: PSI N=100+ rerun (after W2's psi adapter; budget-bound)
;;   W7: ultimatum (operator + cbcl-agent + vanilla + attackers + matrix)
;;   W8: adaptive-attacker library (independent)
;;   W9: DC coalition attacker (independent)
;;   W10: paper integration — Demo 3 update + Demo 5 (ultimatum) + tab
;;        column updates + vanilla-range column
;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

(meta plan
  (id "IMPL-arena-evals")
  (title "Tighten cbcl-arena evaluation: live-LLM × operators × backends, ultimatum, adaptive + coalition attackers, vanilla sweep, N-bump")
  (version "0.1.0")
  (status "active")
  (created "2026-05-01")
  (author "agent:hugo")
  (description "Implement seven evaluation tightenings for the LangSec '26 cbcl-arena artefact: (E1) live-LLM bindings on Yao/Auction/Dining via a generic LlmBackend + ProtocolAdapter refactor; (E2) Claude Sonnet 4.6 + OpenAI GPT-4.1 backends for tab:mcp-attacks columns; (E3) vanilla regex-breadth sweep producing a range column; (E4) PSI live-LLM bump from N=20 to N=100+; (E5) ultimatum operator + attackers + cbcl agent + vanilla agent + measurement-matrix wiring (dialect already ships); (E6) non-stationary (last-K bandit) attacker wrapper; (E7) coalition attacker for DC. Coordinated paper integration in Demo 3 / Demo 5 and tab:mcp-attacks."))

